NAME='Mars'
COVER_SUB='How you act, fight and desire in each sign.'
T=[
('Own sign','Mars is at home in Aries, and Jyotish gives it own-sign and moolatrikona strength: eccentric potential, courage, great activity, exceptional vitality, resistance to pain, a sense of justice and a lightning reaction. Volguine’s red glow, the movement of blood through the whole body, is exactly this. Affection is strong, possessive and sometimes despotic, and the sensuality is overflowing. Karmic reading: a warrior soul that has fought and now learns to fight for something worth it. The shadow is recklessness. The lesson: courage includes patience.'),
('Detriment','Mars in Venus’s house is in detriment, and Jyotish rates Venus neutral to Mars. It gives great vitality, patient tenacity and perseverance that help reach the chosen goal. You are determined and avid in the widest sense, and earnings can be large when Mars is harmonious with Jupiter and the Sun. Under strain, temperament turns passionate, lascivious and unfaithful. Karmic reading: a force learning to wait and to value what it builds. The shadow is a slow-burning rage. The lesson: sometimes the strong thing is to move.'),
('Quick','Mars in Mercury’s sign gives lively intelligence, quick reflexes, analysis and synthesis, remarkable manual skill, many relationships born of charm and initiative, and a love of sport. Jyotish counts Mercury as an enemy of Mars, so the mind and the impulse sometimes fight. With a strained Mars, enemies multiply through a superficial, unreasonable attitude. Karmic reading: a force that learned to fight with words and now learns to choose its battles. The shadow is a sharp tongue. The lesson: pick one fight, or better, one goal.'),
('Fall','Mars is in its fall in Cancer, and Jyotish marks its debilitation here, deepest at 28°. Mars’s imperiousness meets the Moon’s fickleness: the nature is ambitious, but projects are hard to carry out, since after the first impulse comes a tendency to let go. Only with strong harmony from the Sun and Jupiter is the ascent easy. You defend home and family fiercely but through moods and silence. Karmic reading: a force that turns inward and must learn direct speech. The lesson: say what bothers you before it grows.'),
('Bold','Mars in Leo, in the Sun’s house, gives exceptional vitality and a gift for command, though little obedience. There is a pull toward pleasure, adventure, gambling and risk, overflowing but disordered activity, and a lack of sense of measure, with magnanimity toward the defeated. Jyotish counts the Sun as a friend of Mars. Under strain: rash decisions and despotism. Karmic reading: a soul learning to lead by heart. The shadow is arrogance and a bruised ego. The lesson: strength is greater when it protects others.'),
('Precise','Mars in Virgo gives considerable physical endurance and the ability to make great efforts; with Mercury in harmony, balance between thought and action and a peaceful way to settle disputes. A logical mind, constructive criticism and a very developed practical sense. Jyotish counts Mercury as an enemy of Mars. Under strain: enmities and trouble with colleagues. Karmic reading: a force purified through craft and service. The shadow is irritation at details and burnout. The lesson: effort is not always the answer.'),
('Detriment','Mars in Libra, in Venus’s house, is in detriment, and Jyotish rates Venus neutral to Mars. It gives remarkable mental activity, a bent for the arts and for professions linked to justice, and firmness and perseverance on the chosen path. Struggles come hard, but you are not easily discouraged, and with Jupiter and Venus in harmony the difficulties are overcome. You prefer discussion and negotiation, and fight best for others. Karmic reading: a force learning to act for itself. The shadow is passive resistance. The lesson: a fair fight is better than a polite silence.'),
('Own sign','Mars is at home in Scorpio, and Jyotish gives it own-sign strength. Vitality is exceptional, the temperament instinctive and passionate, with no half measures and any means to reach the goal. You face risks with calm and cold blood, but the character is rough, impatient and vengeful. Volguine’s image of the den from which arrows of desire fly fits it well. Karmic reading: a force that passes through death and rebirth. The shadow is control and obsession. The lesson: power is greater when it is used to heal.'),
('Fiery','Mars in Sagittarius gives great mental activity, ambition, audacity and a frankness that borders on tactlessness, with considerable physical strength and endurance. Jyotish counts Jupiter as a friend of Mars. With Jupiter and Saturn in harmony it orients toward active politics: the militant in full action, and sport. Under strain: insolence and quarrelsomeness. Karmic reading: a force seeking a cause worth its energy. The shadow is overconfidence and fanaticism. The lesson: aim carefully before you shoot.'),
('Exalted','Mars is exalted in Capricorn, and Jyotish agrees, placing its peak at 28°. It gives considerable vitality, good resistance to effort and illness, practical sense and ambition that favour realising initiatives. You are bold, do not retreat before obstacles or dangers, and your instinctive, stubborn nature overcomes difficult situations. Karmic reading: a force that has become discipline, building something that lasts. The shadow is workaholism and cold ambition. The lesson: success matters more when someone shares it.'),
('Rebellious','Mars in Aquarius gives, when harmonious or neutral, a very active mind, originality, inventiveness and scientific curiosity with a bent for experiment. Physical resistance is exceptional and activity frenetic. The nature is generous and gentlemanly, busy with many projects and many affairs at once. Jyotish rates Saturn neutral to Mars. Karmic reading: a force that fights for ideals bigger than itself. The shadow is stubborn rebellion and emotional distance. The lesson: a revolution needs allies you keep close.'),
('Diffuse','Mars in Pisces gives a complex behaviour and a double personality: active periods full of initiative alternate with almost total inertia, and boldness gives way to shyness. Sensuality is accentuated, with determination and practical sense when the Sun and Saturn help. Jyotish counts Jupiter as a friend of Mars. Karmic reading: a force that dissolves, learning to act from compassion instead of fear. The shadow is avoidance, escapism and self-sacrifice. The lesson: a gentle will still needs direction.'),
]
